+# TLS backend
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use rustls as the TLS backend, chosen because it is pure Rust and avoids the complexity of C bindings. Certificate verification stays enabled on all builds, including development builds, and https is enforced everywhere with no plaintext exception for any service.
